# ABP Auto API Controllers

ABP automatically generates REST API controllers from application services.

## How It Works
Application services implementing `IRemoteService` interface automatically become API endpoints:
- `IApplicationService` extends `IRemoteService`
- Each method becomes an API endpoint
- HTTP methods determined by naming convention

## HTTP Method Conventions
| Method Prefix | HTTP Method |
|--------------|-------------|
| Get, Find    | GET         |
| Create, Add, Insert | POST |
| Update, Put  | PUT         |
| Delete, Remove | DELETE    |
| Patch        | PATCH       |
| Other        | POST        |

## Route Convention
- `/api/app/{service-name}/{method-name}`
- Example: `BookAppService.GetListAsync` → `GET /api/app/book`

## Customizing Routes
```csharp
[Route("api/my-books")]
public class BookAppService : ApplicationService, IBookAppService
{
    [HttpGet]
    [Route("{id}")]
    public Task<BookDto> GetAsync(Guid id) { }
}
```

## Disabling Auto API
```csharp
[RemoteService(IsEnabled = false)]
public class InternalAppService : ApplicationService { }
```
